@startuml
' Behavior 2 (Figure 5): WAN outage -> Outbox buffering -> reconnect -> replay/catch-up.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: behavior, outage, buffering, replay

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 240

participant "POS Adapter" as POSAD #6FA8DC
participant "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
queue "Outbox" as OB #8E7CC3
participant "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #F1C232
participant "Subscribers" as SUB #F1C232

== WAN link down ==
loop every sale during the outage
  POSAD -> SA : Inventory Event (event stream)
  SA -> SLI : apply (reads and writes continue)
  SA -> OB : append
end
OB -x CFE : publish fails; events held
note over OB : buffers in order; sized for a 30-min\noutage at 100 events/s (~180,000 events)

== WAN link restored ==
OB -> CFE : replay-from-sequence (last acknowledged)\nIEP / TLS 1.3 mutual certs [secure]
CFE --> OB : acknowledge each (acceptedThrough)
note over OB, CFE : catch-up drains at up to 2,000 events/s per store\nwhile live sales keep flowing (PERF-1, PERF-4)
CFE -> SUB : notify (gap filled)
note over SUB : duplicates ignored by event ID;\nresync closes any remaining gap

legend right
  Store-local reads and writes never stop during the
  outage. On reconnect the Outbox replays from the last
  acknowledged sequence, so no event is lost, and drains
  the backlog while live events continue.
endlegend
@enduml
